<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander I of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alexander I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> from 1801 to 1825. He led Russia through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>, including the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s invasion in 1812, and Russian armies reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1814. He played a central role at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>, and his early reforming plans gave way to more conservative rule later in his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia.jpg" alt="Alexander I of Russia" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Dawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_I_of_Russia_by_G.Dawe_(1826,_Peterhof)-crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
